  {
    "title": "API, data and design",
    "body": "**API:** services call `notify(eventId, userId, type)`; users change settings through a preferences API. **Data:** preferences per user, channel and category, with quiet hours and time zone; a **notification ID** (event, user), and `attempts(notification ID, channel)` as primary key with a state: claimed, sent, delivered or failed; device tokens and addresses. **High-level design:** events arrive on a queue with at-least-once delivery; workers turn each event into a message on a queue per channel and priority; **senders**, with one pacer per provider, take each message after its wait in the queue, claim its attempt, read preferences, and send.",
