  {
    "title": "The same event twice",
    "body": "The event queue delivers at least once, so \"order 123 shipped\" can reach two workers, and two copies of the email land on the email queue. Without a check, each copy is sent: the user gets **two**. Instead, the sender first inserts the attempt (order123:u42, email) into `attempts` as claimed. The primary key accepts the first insert and rejects the second, so only one copy is sent. Attempts are kept 7 days; the event queue redelivers an event for at most 2 days and workers skip older events, so a key is never needed after it expires. That is about 3 GB of attempts a day.",
