  {
    "title": "A crash after sending",
    "body": "A sender claims an email attempt, sends it, and crashes before marking it sent. When the message is redelivered, the attempt is still \"claimed\", and nobody knows whether the provider got the email. **Send again**, and the user may get two; **don't**, and the user may get none. The email provider accepts an **idempotency key** and drops a repeat with the same key for 24 hours: the retry passes the attempt key, so the provider drops the repeat. Push has no such key, so a claimed push is never sent again: a rare miss. SMS login codes are sent first and recorded after, so they err on a rare duplicate, the stated exception, because a missing code locks the user out.",
